# **the IR is the point of this case, and the OUT section is not enough.** measured: with the
# promotion suppressed the program still printed `<7|hi|1.50>` here, LLVM's AArch64 lowering having
# promoted the variadic tail itself. that is one backend being generous down a path no C compiler
# generates, so the `sext`/`fpext` this compiler emits - the same ones Clang emits - are asserted
# directly rather than inferred from a value that survives either way

--- OUT --->
11
<7|hi|1.50>
5
plain
--- IR --->
# the declaration is variadic, which is the whole of what `variadic_args` buys - the tail parameter
# is no parameter at all in LLVM
CHECK: declare i32 @snprintf(ptr, i64, ptr, ...)

# C's default argument promotions, applied by AST::CallResolver and emitted with no second opinion
# from codegen
CHECK: fpext float
CHECK: call i32 (ptr, i64, ptr, ...) @snprintf(ptr

# and an empty list really is no arguments at all
CHECK: call i32 (ptr, i64, ptr, ...) @snprintf(ptr
